{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has a single obligation. `Criterion::source_node_id` must return the `NodeId<D>` of the criterion's source node, which is the node the criterion is evaluated on.\n\nTwo marked tests cover it:\n\n- **Contracts test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` builds a `Review` on node `Node(1)`. Its `Criterion::source_node_id` returns the stored `source`. The test asserts that the verified evidence's `source_node_id()` equals the interned `Node(1)`. After a store and load round trip, it asserts that the loaded evidence's `source_node_id()` still equals the original. This exercises the trait method indirectly, through the evidence the runtime builds from it.\n- **SDK test:** `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` calls the trait method directly on a real `Review` criterion. It asserts `review().source_node_id() == node`, where `node` is the interned requirement node. The test then stores the evidence and loads it again under that same node. That load would fail if the criterion reported a different source node. This holds even though the record has non-empty dependencies, which matches the `source_node` definition: tracked reads of other nodes do not change the source node.\n\nThe direct assertion in the SDK test and the evidence-level assertions in the contracts test together catch an implementation that returns the wrong node. The requirement states no failure cases or boundaries beyond this, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "591b313492c443ed1884725db73bf42bdd8629e2dc34d0a29a2f1a52c75c882d",
